ent so they run  down to grab the cameras and see what  was on the cameras they open up these  lock boxes and then like all the  electronics are missing and the cameras  and they're like wait what like these  were locked up and who took it's like a  game and so it gets really interesting  where  is it a game i don't know but it might  be a consciousness thing and so  i get passionate about a place like that  because it gives you the ability to do  to really jump into some wild stuff i  mean one of the scientists there  was walking through a field  and they basically saw um you know they  saw they walked past um  like a cow or something and then they  turn around it was gone  and then like 10 minutes later they're  like where is it they turn back around  and there it is on the ground just out  of nowhere with like two broken legs so  they run in the ground  for life  it was no it was alive you know and then  they run back into the the house to go  grab a gun or something to take care of  it and when they come out now it has  four broken legs you know or something  it's like creepy and and and like  causing  alarm because  number one it makes no sense number two  it's like it's happening so quick that  they can't even um and i got family  showing up from the beach you know you  see people behind me but um you  mentioned the beach they all went to the  beach earlier but um  what it seems to be is that it's it's  you know an issue with  time  um and an issue with  moving it like from here to here where  we can't see it and back and then people  see crap and then i don't know it's  it's just wild and it and it's so  fascinating and i always tell people in  hollywood because you know to start  getting into making like  movies and tv series and documentaries  and stuff and i just you don't need to  sensationalize this stuff you don't need  to come up with  um  like like science fiction type um  you know ideas to make it intriguing i  mean it's it is it's it's wild the way 